 "notes": "Annual Review (Adelberger, Heckel & Nelson 2003). Headline result is Figure 5 ('midlam.eps'): 95%-CL constraints on ISL-violating Yukawa interactions |alpha| vs range lambda for 1 um < lambda < 1 cm. Reported curve is the lower boundary of the shaded 'excluded region', i.e. the envelope of the heavy experimental upper-limit curves (Eot-Wash combined 2-experiment result presented by this group, Colorado/Long, Stanford/Chiaverini, Lamoreaux, Irvine); the Eot-Wash combined limit is new in this review (refs 148,149 are its own conference proceedings). Extracted from EPS vector segments; axes calibrated from tick marks (x: 3 units/decade from 1e-6 m; y: 0.7715 units/decade from 1e-4). Mass converted via m = 1.97e-7 eV*m / lambda, so mass range 1.97e-5 eV (lambda=1 cm, Irvine, alpha=5.2e-4) to 8.1e-2 eV (lambda=2.4e-6 m, alpha~1e10). Native |alpha| kept rather than converting to g_N (conversion would be g_N = m_N*sqrt(4*pi*alpha)/(1.22e19 GeV) assuming coupling to nucleon number). Cross-check: envelope crosses alpha=16/3 at lambda~130 um, matching the text's Eot-Wash statement. Longer-range constraints (Fig 4, lambda>1 cm) and less-rigorous Casimir-range constraints (Fig 9, lambda<1 um, adapted from another reference) not included.",
